    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA detached five-bedroom bungalow extending to approximately 151 sq m (1,625 sq ft), set on a mature site of 0.20 Ha (0.49 acre) with generous lawned gardens to both front and rear.\n\nPositioned off the N56 in the heart of Letterkenny, the property is within walking distance of Optum, PGIM, Tata Consultancy Services and Letterkenny University Hospital, and within easy reach of Main Street, primary and secondary schools, and the full range of the town's amenities.\n\nThe house is suitable for immediate occupation however would benefit from modernisation and refurbishment and represents an excellent opportunity for a purchaser with vision to create a superb family home in a highly convenient town-centre location. Accommodation extends to an entrance porch, entrance hall, two sitting rooms, an open-plan living and dining room, kitchen, five bedrooms, a shower room and an ensuite wet room.\n\nThe property benefits from mains water and sewer connections, oil-fired central heating, an open fireplace in the front sitting room and a Stanley stove in the living room. Glazing is a mix of hardwood single-glazed and PVC double-glazed windows throughout.\n\nThe site extends to 0.20 Ha (0.49 acres) of mature gardens with ample space for parking, and offers potential for those wishing to explore the creation of additional habitable accommodation, subject to the necessary planning consents. \n\nThe property should qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, providing a further financial incentive for prospective purchasers. Enquiries regarding grant eligibility should be made directly with Donegal County Council."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 10.08m ×1.40m\nSeating area.\n\nEntrance Hall - 4.48m × 1.22m\nCarpet flooring.\n\nSitting Room - 4.41m × 3.56m\nCarpet flooring. Gas fireplace with tiled hearth, surround and mantelpiece.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.98m × 3.56m\nCarpet flooring. Built-in double wardrobe. Open fireplace with tiled surround, hearth and mantelpiece.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.52m × 3.28m\nCarpet flooring. Built-in wardrobes.\n\nPlus - 0.98m × 0.48m\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.27m × 2.46m\nCarpet flooring.\n\nShower Room - 2.13m × 1.67m\nLarge shower enclosure with mains shower. Tiled floor and fully tiled walls.\n\nHot Press / Storage - 3.27m × 1.85m\nLaminate timber flooring.\n\nSitting Room / Dining Room - 5.63m × 4.70m\nCarpet flooring. Stanley range.\n\nPlus - 2.40m × 0.95m\n\n\nKitchen - 2.91m × 2.81m\nWall and base units. Zanussi grill and electric oven. Four-burner gas hob. Plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher. Freestanding Bosch fridge-freezer.\n\nInner Bedroom Hall - 0.91m × 4.38m\nLaminate flooring.\n\nStoreroom - 2.00m × 1.06m\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.59m × 3.02m\nLaminate flooring.\n\nEnsuite Wet Room - 1.93m × 3.20m\nVinyl floor covering. Fully tiled walls. Electric Triton T90Z shower. WC. WHB.\n\nBack Hall - 2.77m × 1.20m\nDoor to rear garden.\n\nBedroom 5 - 2.83m × 2.59m\nCarpet flooring.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 5 beds, 2 bathrooms, 2 reception rooms.</li><li> Large front and rear gardens.</li><li> Easy reach of Letterkenny town. </li><li> Constructed in the 1960's and extended in the 1980's.</li><li> Vacant homes Refurbishment Grant available.</li><li> SEAI Grants available.</li><li> Stanley stove heats the radiators.</ul>"
      },
